<section id="the-idea" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="the-idea">The idea</h2>
<p>A <strong>star schema</strong> puts one big <em>fact</em> table (events you measure, like sales) in the middle, surrounded by small <em>dimension</em> tables (who, what, where, when).</p>
<table class="caption-top table">
<colgroup>
<col style="width: 50%">
<col style="width: 50%">
</colgroup>
<thead>
<tr class="header">
<th>Table</th>
<th>Example columns</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr class="odd">
<td><code>fact_sales</code></td>
<td><code>date_id</code>, <code>product_id</code>, <code>store_id</code>, <code>quantity</code>, <code>revenue</code></td>
</tr>
<tr class="even">
<td><code>dim_product</code></td>
<td><code>product_id</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>category</code>, <code>brand</code></td>
</tr>
<tr class="odd">
<td><code>dim_store</code></td>
<td><code>store_id</code>, <code>city</code>, <code>country</code></td>
</tr>
<tr class="even">
<td><code>dim_date</code></td>
<td><code>date_id</code>, <code>day</code>, <code>month</code>, <code>year</code>, <code>is_holiday</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</section>
<section id="a-query" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="a-query">A query</h2>
